# Comments belong in the docs

Unfurnished and the repo docs hold the why. Name the code so it reads without a caption.

Put intent, design, and usage in the repo docs (`AGENTS.md`, `README`, design docs).

On a line you are already editing, a narration comment leaves with the edit. Move a sentence to the docs only when it records intent the docs lack.

A comment stays when it is one of these:

- A license or generated-file header
- A formatter or lint directive
- A doc comment on a public API, or a comment a compiler, type checker, or build tool reads
- One line naming an external constraint (dependency, platform, or protocol) and nothing else
